@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] asset-folder-shape
Every asset MUST be one folder, named in kebab case: `assets/<group>/<asset-name>/` (groups such as
`characters/` and `animations/`), or `assets/world/` for the one world. It holds exactly:
`asset.toml` (its kind, settings and inputs checksum), `src/` (every input of its export), and what its
kind's exporter writes: `<asset-name>.glb` (`<asset-name>.ktx2` for a texture), plus the outputs that kind
declares (the world's `tiles/`).
Nothing else MAY sit in an asset folder. Folders inside `src/` follow the kind's layout (the world's
`src/ground/` and `src/regions/<region>/`).

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] asset-src-is-the-asset
An asset's folder MUST hold what that asset is: its source files and code in `src/`, and its own numbers
in `asset.toml`. A `.rs` file in `src/` MUST express those choices through the exporter's traits, methods and helpers, and
MUST NOT define a general method another asset could use: that belongs in `tools/export/`. It MUST NOT
read or change another asset's `src/`. A character's changes to an animation MUST be numbers in its own
`asset.toml`, in the table that animation's file defines, never code in the character or the animation.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] exports-never-edited
An asset's exports MUST be written only by `cargo export`, never by hand, and MUST be committed together
with the settings and sources they were exported from, with a current inputs checksum.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] world-ground-has-one-owner
The world's ground MUST be one grid of heights, in the pages under `assets/world/src/ground/`. A region
MUST NOT bring its own ground. It adds to the world only through the exporter's `Region` trait: what it
lays over the ground, and, as declared changes, how it reshapes the ground inside its own area.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:performance] textures-are-named-not-copied
A texture more than one asset shows MUST be its own asset under `assets/textures/<name>/`, exported as a `.ktx2`
with every mipmap level. Another asset's export MUST point at that file by a relative path and never hold a copy,
and its checksum MUST cover the texture's name but not its bytes, so repainting a texture rebuilds nothing else.
A texture only one asset shows stays inside that asset.
